### Q2. Why is Randomized Quick Sort more preferable? Write its pseudocode.

**Advantages:**
1. Reduces dependence on the original input arrangement.
2. Provides O(n log n) expected time complexity.
3. Reduces the likelihood of repeatedly selecting poor pivots.
4. Works efficiently for different input arrangements.

**Pseudocode:**

```text
RANDOMIZED-QUICKSORT(A, low, high)

    If low < high:

        Choose a random pivot

        Exchange pivot with last element

        p = PARTITION(A, low, high)

        RANDOMIZED-QUICKSORT(A, low, p-1)

        RANDOMIZED-QUICKSORT(A, p+1, high)
```

